This subroutines allow the use of libxc (https://libxc.gitlab.io/)
instead of the subroutines included with the cpw2000 code.
Just compile this subroutines with the main program BEFORE linking to the libpw library.

They replace the four entry points of the exchange and correlation in Src/ALFA:

   xc_lda_libxc.f90        xc_lda         CA=PZ, VWN, WI, PW92 (libxc 9, 7, 2, 13) with LDA_X (1)
   xc_gga_libxc.f90        xc_gga         PBE (libxc 101 and 130)
   xc_mgga_libxc.f90       xc_mgga        LAK (342, 345), TASK (707 with PW92 13), R2SC (497, 498)
   xc_mgga_vxc_libxc.f90   xc_mgga_vxc    TB09=TBL (208), BR (from 208 with c = 2/3)

Functionals are identified by their numbers, which work with libxc 5, 6 and 7.
In libxc 7 the named constants (XC_LDA_X, ...) are in the module xc_f03_funcs_m.

Here are examples that you can change according to your directory structure,
with libxc installed in $HOME/other_codes, and from the Src directory

 ifx -qopenmp -xHost -O3 cpw_variables.f90 cpw.f90 $HOME/other_codes/include/libxcf03.f90 ../Tools/LIBXC/*.f90  \
     libpw_ifx.a $HOME/other_codes/lib/libxc.a -qmkl -o cpw_libxc.exe

 gfortran -fopenmp -O3 cpw_variables.f90 cpw.f90 $HOME/other_codes/include/libxcf03.f90 ../Tools/LIBXC/*.f90  \
     libpw_gfortran.a $HOME/other_codes/lib/libxc.a -lopenblas -lpthread -lgomp -o cpw_libxc.exe

and the same with cpw_post_process.f90.

you need the modules from libxcf03.f90, compiled with the same compiler as cpw2000.
The .mod files installed by libxc only work with the compiler that compiled libxc.
In the libxc build directory libxcf03.f90 is src/libxcf03.f90 (remove the lines
starting with # if the compiler complains).

Comparison with the native subroutines (WORK/xc_test/test_xc_grid.f90, libxc 7.1.2,
November 2026), largest relative difference on a grid of rho, s, alpha:

   LDA, LAK, TASK, R2SC, TB09, BR     1E-13 or better for alpha > 0
   PBE                                4E-6, the native version uses beta and gamma
                                      of the original paper, libxc more digits

By default libxc enforces sigma <= 8 rho tau (Fermi hole curvature), which changes
the results where tau < tau_W (alpha < 0).  The native subroutines do not, and
neither do these ones (LFHC = .FALSE. in xc_mgga_libxc.f90 and xc_mgga_vxc_libxc.f90).
alpha < 0 appears with numerical noise (low cutoff with a core kinetic energy
density) and systematically in the Thomas-Fermi deorbitalized versions (R2TF, LATF,
TATF).  Where tau <= 0 libxc uses its tau threshold, so results differ there.
At alpha = 0 exactly libxc LAK and TASK use the left limit of the derivatives,
the native subroutines the right limit.

You have to implement yourself other functionals if you want.
Check the elk code (https://elk.sourceforge.io/) for inspiration, as it looks neat
and similar to the present case.
